{
  "id": "COMPOUND:16006 - PROTEIN:6078",
  "verbalization": "Spiroquinazoline is implicated in the regulation of Forkhead box protein O1 (FoxO1) through a multi-step mechanism involving splicing factors. The evidence suggests that Spiroquinazoline acts as a target for D-Tryptophan and another compound, 2-(3-Hydroxy-5-methoxyphenyl)-3-methoxyfuro[2,3-h]chromen-4-one, both of which ultimately target FoxO1. This indicates that Spiroquinazoline may influence FoxO1 through a pathway involving splicing factors, which are themselves targets of these compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Spiroquinazoline in modulating FoxO1 activity via splicing factor-mediated signaling. The evidence supports a dependency on these splicing factors, suggesting that Spiroquinazoline may act as a modulator of FoxO1 through a complex network of targets.",
